kosha velocity-plan

  -- choosing angular-velocity for each joint given a trajectory
  -- P = E / T: power and time trade off via path-energy
  -- T* = sqrt(E): the balanced optimum where T* = P* (minimises both simultaneously)
  -- three modes: minimize-T (fastest, at rated omega), minimize-P (slow, T >> T*),
  -- balanced (T = T*, P = P* = sqrt(E))

  "mechanical-energy-varga-vishesa"
  "tinanta-swarupa bhave-prayoga-swarupa"

  -- sangati roots: kaala (the time budget T), viveka (discriminating which goal
  -- to optimise), gati (the motion whose velocities are being planned),
  -- seema (T* = sqrt(E) is the threshold between time-dominated and power-dominated)
  "kaala-yukta gati-swarupa viveka-siddha"
  "seema-yukta path-energy-abheda"
  "angular-velocity-phala trajectory-sthita"
  "power-apeksha time-apeksha"

done
